<%= colour_palette('web') %>

## Functional colours

A functional colour has one job. Use it only for that job, and use the palette for anything else.

- Use `inverse-text` for text on dark backgrounds.
- Use `template-background` for the page behind the content and `body-background` for the content area.
- Use `focus` only for the element that has keyboard focus.
- Use `error` only for error messages and `success` only for success messages.
- Use `hover` only for the hover state of inputs.

